  "notes": "Only the compact front section is modelled. Door/frame/handle plus the fixed glass child have a combined moving mass of exactly 4 kg: frame 3.316 kg, glass 0.684 kg. The untextured door_window inherits the door slide; do not add a second joint. The 180 mm handle bar centreline is X=-60 mm, 30 mm proud of the X=-30 door face; its outer surface reaches X=-70, so the complete closed prop is 770 X, not 700. A 2 mm general edge radius cannot fit 1.5 mm sheet: thin-stock edges use R0.3, while solid enclosure trim, the plinth, door and panel use R2. The prescribed 120 x 90 screen and 60 mm emergency disc at Z1180 cannot share the top of a 150 mm-wide panel without overlap. The screen is immediately below the emergency disc, Z1052-1142; emergency, button and panel positions are preserved. All seven panel library components are appended, copied and rigidly transformed from the existing Task 2 source; original 1024 atlases are copied byte-for-byte, not rebaked. Press direction is +X; the two-position selector rotates about outward -X, inheriting its detents and recommended initial MAN angle. All main machine atlases are 2048. The specified one-piece table collider fills visual T slots. The specified two spindle proxies cover head and nose, omitting the narrow holder/cutter. Specified door proxies omit small handle standoffs. Coolant streaks and solid curled aluminium chips are visual. Jaw serrations use a 1.8 mm diagonal colour pattern and 0.18 mm source-PBR relief. Jaw mass, damping=2 and frictionloss=1 were unspecified benchmark choices. Automatic clamping, interlocks, button springs, e-stop latch and selector detents are simulator contracts in metadata, not a demonstrated machining controller. The parallels' 80 mm length runs along Y, parallel to the jaw faces, at X90 and X110; this leaves both parallels clear of the complete jaw stroke. No workpiece is fused to this prop: place either separate bar at [0.100,0,0.860]. The suggested X=340 world placement puts the workpiece at X440 but the handle at X280, outside the stated X300-480 ideal reach. Use a phased scene: X360 machine placement puts the initial handle at X300 and part at X460; the complete Y460 door stroke takes its handle through the gap between the two hands' preferred Y bands. The emergency centre Z1180 is also above the Z800-1000 preferred band. Exact geometry is retained; scene-level reach and regrasp planning remain necessary. Metres, Z up, front -X, applied transforms and a common prop frame. Triangulated OBJ, 30-degree smoothing and weighted normals. Smart UV 66 degrees, nonoverlapping islands, 0.01 margins. CPU Cycles 64-sample DIFFUSE COLOR * (0.4 + 0.6 * AO), RGB8 sRGB, excluding direct illumination and highlights. Full Principled PBR and original printing images are packed in source.blend. Preview: CPU Cycles 64, 1024 square, neutral grey, three area lights, front-left above. Per-instance colour multipliers of 0.97-1.03 may be applied by simulation.  Task 13 compact OBJ exception: positions use 5 decimal metres where safe; necessary vertices retain up to 6 decimals to preserve nonzero triangles, strict collision convexity and the 0.005 mm Euclidean movement bound. Independent fixed-5 rounding cannot satisfy all three. Normals/UVs use 4 decimals; every original triangle, position index and per-corner attribute value is retained. Equal rounded UV records share indices and visual OBJ indices use shorter equivalent relative notation. No collision remeshing, reindexing or simplification. Task 13 delivery: baked albedos are Lanczos-downsampled to at most 1024 px except the unchanged-resolution factory-floor repeat tile; previews are 512 square. PNG encoding uses RGB8 or reviewed 256-colour Floyd-Steinberg palettes; source artwork pixels and source.blend are retained. Shared PNG paths resolve from this prop folder.",
